  "about": "Searches for the heading inventory (tests/inventory.js). Chosen from outside sources rather than by hand, so no kind of results page is missed. Selection rule: (1) every distinct search in the top 40 of either US volume list, near-duplicates merged (\"chat gpt\" into \"chatgpt\", \"ig\" into \"instagram\"); (2) ranks 41-100 sampled once per kind of site or topic not already covered; (3) the top questions, one per question type (many are 'where to watch <team> vs <team>', so one of those); (4) Google's Year in Search 2025 US categories, one or two per category; (5) one search per Google rich-result feature that none of the above shows; (6) the standard set from tests/queries.json.",
